          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>w</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle N_{w}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d0671b383d3eee32025f08d4bdceae2e6d059258" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:3.275ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle N_{w}}"/></span> are the number densities of ice and liquid particles (respectively), and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt22" id="mwPw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\bar{r_i}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle {\bar {r_{i}}}}">
  <semantics>
